        '''# The Moon and the Pot of Stars\n\nLong ago, the moon was a woman named Njema who loved the earth so much that she wanted to give it a gift. She went to the creator and asked for a pot filled with stars.\n\n"These stars will light the night for the people below," she said. "So they can travel safely, find their way home, and tell stories under the sky."\n\nThe creator gave her the pot, and Njema climbed to the highest point of the sky. She poured the stars across the darkness, and they scattered like seeds of light.\n\nBut some stars fell into the river, and the fish were amazed. Some fell into the forest, and the animals gathered to watch. Some fell into the villages, and the children reached up to try to catch them.\n\nNjema smiled. "Now the night will never be truly dark," she said. "And every story told under the stars will carry a piece of my love for the earth."\n\nThat is why, the elders say, the moon shines brightest when she is full — because her heart is full of love for the world below. And the stars twinkle because they carry the stories of all who look up at them.\n\n**Moral:** Love inspires us to share our gifts with the world, lighting the way for others.''',
